diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..a969c8b 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -40,6 +40,32 @@ bin/dev # You need to start the dev server in the same terminal session
 
 This will ask for your 1password authorization to read and set the environment variables that Stripe needs.
 
+### Plans
+
+| Plan | Price | Cards | Storage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Free | $0 | 1,000 | 1 GB |
+| Unlimited | $20/month | Unlimited | 5 GB |
+| Unlimited+ | $25/month | Unlimited | 500 GB |
+
+The plans live in `saas/app/models/plan.rb`. Each paid plan reads its Stripe price
+from the environment (`STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` and
+`STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID`), so every Stripe environment can point
+at its own prices.
+
+Stripe hosts checkout and the customer portal, and posts subscription changes to
+`/stripe/webhooks`, verified with `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. What comes back is
+mirrored onto `Account::Subscription` so plan lookups never need a round trip.
+
+A free account that runs out of cards can still draft, but publishing and creating
+through the API are refused, and the create buttons give way to an upgrade pitch.
+
+### Support tools
+
+`/admin/accounts` lists the accounts. An account page can be comped (billed
+nothing, held to no limits), and its card count and bytes used can be overridden
+to reproduce or relieve a limit without touching the real data.
+
 ### Stripe environments
 
 * [Development](https://dashboard.stripe.com/acct_1SdTFtRus34tgjsJ/test/dashboard)
